From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nydal91 <nydal91@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:53:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/17] Add SGSR 2 upscaler backend for DX11

Port the 2-pass compute variant of Snapdragon Game Super Resolution 2 to
HLSL and expose it as the sgsr2 Dx11Upscaler. It's aimed at Adreno GPUs,
where FSR's compute workload is expensive.

NGX provides full per-pixel motion vectors, so these replace upstream's
camera reprojection, which needs matrices NGX doesn't supply. For the same
reason all 9 color samples are always taken.

MSBuild compiles the shaders, so no precompiled bytecode is committed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A9WqnwGsLAcGJXd49N2pes
